  "summary": "A hybrid interior style fusing Scandinavian coziness with Japanese wabi-sabi restraint: light wood, low furniture, muted earth tones.",
  "description": "Japandi crystallized in the 2010s as designers merged hygge comfort with Japanese minimal discipline: low platforms, paper lanterns, pale oak, clay ceramics and unbleached textiles. Neither strictly Zen nor strictly Scandi, it favors imperfect handmade objects and decluttered calm. Popularized through design media and Pinterest, it is a documented commercial hybrid of two established traditions.",
